WPE without libdrm: the one DRM format code the UI process names

The UI process's backing store compares a DMA-BUF buffer's format with
DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888 when it takes a snapshot, and includes DRM's header
of formats only with libdrm (USE_LIBDRM). A port without libdrm -
ThreadOS has neither DRM nor DMA-BUF - does not compile. The code is
defined where the header is not: the fourcc 'X' 'R' '2' '4', as
drm_fourcc.h has it.

--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/wpe/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/wpe/AcceleratedBackingStore.cpp
@@ -41,6 +41,10 @@
 #include <drm/drm_fourcc.h>
 #elif USE(LIBDRM)
 #include <drm_fourcc.h>
+#else
+// Without libdrm there is no header of DRM's formats, and no DMA-BUF
+// buffer either; the one code compared with below is XRGB8888's
+#define DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888 0x34325258 // 'X' 'R' '2' '4'
 #endif
 
 WTF_IGNORE_WARNINGS_IN_THIRD_PARTY_CODE_BEGIN
